# NEXORA CRM — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust for the target host. Never commit the real .env
# (it is git-ignored). On the deployment host DATABASE_URL MUST point to an
# absolute path on persistent storage.

# --- Required ---
# SQLite database. Use an ABSOLUTE path on persistent storage in production,
# e.g. file:/var/lib/nexora/custom.db
# (Local development default: file:./db/custom.db — see .env on the dev box.)
DATABASE_URL="file:/var/lib/nexora/custom.db"

# --- Runtime ---
# Set automatically by `next start` / the standalone server. Do not set
# NODE_ENV manually unless running behind a process manager that does not:
# production mode also DISABLES the demo-seed endpoint (POST /api/v1/dev/seed
# returns 404) and switches session cookies to Secure when the reverse proxy
# sends X-Forwarded-Proto: https.
# NODE_ENV=production

# --- Email delivery (NOT CONFIGURED — reserved for the future provider) ---
# No email flows are active today: member invitations provision accounts
# directly (admin-only) and there is no password-reset endpoint. When an
# email provider is chosen, define its credentials HERE — do not hard-code
# them. The variable names below are placeholders to be adapted to the
# chosen provider; do not fill them with invented values.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=            # e.g. smtp | resend | ses (decided at setup time)
# EMAIL_FROM=                # verified sender address, e.g. noreply@your-domain
# EMAIL_SMTP_HOST=
# EMAIL_SMTP_PORT=
# EMAIL_SMTP_USER=
# EMAIL_SMTP_PASSWORD=
